# Rocket Fi - Environment Variables Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual values
# Never commit your .env file to version control

# =============================================================================
# REQUIRED - OpenRouter API Configuration
# =============================================================================
# Get your API key from: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Required for AI-powered financial analysis and retirement planning insights
# 
# IMPORTANT: OpenRouter API keys must start with 'sk-or-v1-'
# Example format: sk-or-v1-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# The app will show "string did not match expected pattern" if your key format is wrong
VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your-openrouter-api-key-here

# =============================================================================
# OPTIONAL - Development Configuration
# =============================================================================
# Uncomment and modify these if needed for your specific setup

# Development server port (default: 5173)
# VITE_PORT=5173

# Base URL for production builds
# VITE_BASE_URL=https://yourdomain.com

# =============================================================================
# SECURITY NOTES
# =============================================================================
# - This is a client-side application, so API keys will be visible in the browser
# - For production, consider implementing a backend proxy for API calls
# - The OpenRouter free tier has rate limits - monitor your usage
# - User data is encrypted locally in browser storage using AES encryption

# =============================================================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# =============================================================================
# 1. Create a new .env file by copying this file:
#    cp .env.sample .env
#
# 2. Sign up for OpenRouter at https://openrouter.ai/
# 3. Generate a new API key from your dashboard
# 4. Replace 'sk-or-v1-your-openrouter-api-key-here' with your actual key
# 5. Save the file
#
# Available free models you can use:
# - google/gemma-3-27b-it:free
# - google/gemma-2-9b-it:free  
# - mistralai/mistral-7b-instruct:free
# - meta-llama/llama-3-8b-instruct:free
# - microsoft/phi-3-medium-128k-instruct:free
#
# =============================================================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# =============================================================================
# If you get "API Key is missing" errors:
# - Verify your .env file exists in the project root directory
# - Ensure the VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY variable is set
# - Restart your development server after adding the .env file
# - Check that your OpenRouter key has sufficient credits
#
# If you get "The string did not match the expected pattern" errors:
# - Verify your OpenRouter API key starts with 'sk-or-v1-'
# - Check your browser's developer console (F12) for detailed error messages
# - Ensure your OpenRouter account is active and has API access
# - Try generating a new API key from your OpenRouter dashboard
# - Check if your API key has the correct permissions for the models you're using
# - Use the debugging tools I've added to check the API key format
#
# If AI analysis isn't working:
# - Verify your OpenRouter API key is valid and active
# - Check the browser console for detailed error messages
# - Ensure you have internet connectivity for API calls
# - Try using one of the recommended free models listed above
# - I've added debug logging - check the browser console for detailed info
# - Use the api-test.js script to test your API key outside the browser
#
# DEBUGGING STEPS:
# 1. Open browser developer tools (F12)
# 2. Go to the Reports & Insights page
# 3. Click "Start AI Analysis"
# 4. Check the Console tab for detailed debug output
# 5. Look for "API Key Debug Info" and "OpenRouter Response Status" messages
# 6. Share the full error messages if you need further assistance
#
# EXTERNAL API TESTING:
# Run this command to test your API key directly:
# node -r dotenv/config api-test.js